dxdb
====

dxdb is a Rust reimplementation of RxDB, an unaffiliated port of its
Apache-2.0 core with independently specified replacements for its paid
features.

Portions of this work are derived from RxDB (https://github.com/pubkey/rxdb),
which is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. The upstream copyright
notice is preserved here as required by Section 4(c) and 4(d) of that license:

    Copyright 2015-2025 Netflix, Inc., Microsoft Corp. and contributors

Upstream source pin: pubkey/rxdb at commit
3b763ee17d62bc96cfae556ea0ccf92f9891c8c1 (2026-10-25), version 17.6.0.

Crates under crates/cleanroom/ are NOT derived from upstream. They are
independently specified from public documentation only; no upstream
closed-source or premium source was consulted in their design or
implementation. See docs/CLEANROOM.md.

dxdb is not endorsed by, affiliated with, or connected to RxDB's maintainer.
"RxDB" is used only to describe provenance.

